0..49 Comment "//! This source defines the pure lambda calculus."
50..53 Comment "//!"
54..134 Comment "//! `LC` has one substitution. It is the single-substitution calculus of § 7 of"
135..228 Comment "//! [Kaposi-2024-secondorder_generalised_algebraic_theories_signatures_firstorder_semantics]."
229..306 Comment "//! It is the presentation that `first_order` mints from `theory Lambda`. Its"
307..385 Comment "//! names omit the generated `$`, and its context arguments are implicit, as a"
386..417 Comment "//! `theory` block writes them."
418..421 Comment "//!"
422..501 Comment "//! The source uses de Bruijn indices. `Lift` is a substitution constructor, so"
502..581 Comment "//! the substitution laws reach their inductive steps by conversion. Lifting as"
582..616 Comment "//! a definition reaches them too."
617..620 Comment "//!"
621..636 Comment "//! - see: #640"
637..653 Comment "//! - see: #2422"
654..755 Comment "//! - cites: [Kaposi-2024-secondorder_generalised_algebraic_theories_signatures_firstorder_semantics]"
756..759 Comment "//!"
760..959 Comment "//! [Kaposi-2024-secondorder_generalised_algebraic_theories_signatures_firstorder_semantics]: https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10 \"Kaposi and Xie, Second-Order Generalised Algebraic Theories\""
961..1000 Comment "// The naturals, the de Bruijn indices."
